---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Who I am, how I work, and what I'm looking for next."
>
  <article class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Cris Arji</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        One paragraph on what you build and who you build it for. Replace this.
      </p>

      <p>
        A second paragraph on how you work — the kind of problems you like, the
        kind of team you do your best work on, what you reach for by default and
        what you argue against.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm looking for</h2>
      <p>
        Say it plainly. A reader who has got this far is deciding whether to
        email you, and vagueness here is what stops them.
      </p>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <ul class="links">
        <li>
          <a href="mailto:crisarji@gmail.com">crisarji@gmail.com</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/crisarji" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem); }
  h1 { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .prose { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .lede { font-size: var(--t-lg); }
  h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .links { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .links li + li { margin-top: 0.35rem; }
</style>
